# SYNOPSIS

```usage
vx build [arch ...]
vx test [arch ...]
vx boot [arch]
```

# DESCRIPTION

These commands drive CMake's per-arch trees, `build/<arch>/`, which the presets in `CMakePresets.json` configure.
An <arch> is `amd64`, `arm64` or `rv64`.

`vx build` configures each <arch> given, once, and builds it.
With none it builds all three.
A tree is configured when it has no `build.ninja`; after that only the build runs.

`vx test` builds each <arch>, then runs that arch's QEMU tests with `ctest`, one arch after another and never two at once: under the load of two suites, rv64's boots outlast their timeouts.
With no <arch> it tests `amd64` and `arm64`.
The `rv64` suite is off by default; naming it runs it.
It stops at the first arch whose build or tests fail, and exits 1.

`vx boot` builds one <arch> (`amd64` by default) and boots it interactively in QEMU, with edk2 firmware from `/usr/share/edk2`, by running `ninja -C build/<arch> run`.
Ctrl-A x quits QEMU.
More than one <arch> is refused.

Each step's output goes to `build/vx/<arch>-configure.log`, `<arch>-build.log` or `<arch>-test.log`.
`vx boot`'s own run is not logged: it owns the terminal.

# FILES

: `build/<arch>/`
  The CMake tree.
: `build/vx/*.log`
  Each step's output.
: `CMakePresets.json`
  The presets, one per arch.

